Falsifies `byte_sink_contract::verification::end_of_stream_is_no_bytes_message`.

The defect: `end_of_stream` is built with the bytes opcode, so the end-of-stream first word equals an empty
bytes message and a sink cannot tell the writer is finished.

Expected to fail: the harness's claim that `end_of_stream()` differs from `first_word(OPERATION_BYTES, n)`; Kani
reports it failing at a count of 0.

diff --git a/crates/byte_sink_contract/src/lib.rs b/crates/byte_sink_contract/src/lib.rs
index cd68507..5ceea85 100644
--- a/crates/byte_sink_contract/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/byte_sink_contract/src/lib.rs
@@ -124,7 +124,7 @@ pub const fn len(word_zero: u64) -> usize {
 /// kept as a documentation alias.
 #[doc(alias = "eof")]
 pub const fn end_of_stream() -> u64 {
-    first_word(OPERATION_END_OF_STREAM, 0)
+    first_word(OPERATION_BYTES, 0)
 }
 
